 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## smallpt browser experiment
+
+The home page is a prerendered `index.html` containing a client-only WebAssembly
+port of [Kevin Beason's smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) (MIT).
+The original source and license live in `vendor/smallpt/`. `renderer.cpp` keeps
+the original path integrator and adds material setters and batched RGBA output.
+The bundled reference image is the original project's `result_25k.png`; it stays
+visible while the first live render runs. Subsequent renders keep the previous
+image visible until the new render finishes.
+
+- `pnpm install` installs application dependencies.
+- `npm run build` rebuilds Wasm with Emscripten and builds the Astro application.
+- `npm run build:wasm` rebuilds only the Wasm assets. Requires `em++` on PATH
+  (or the `EMXX` environment variable). If Emscripten is absent, the application
+  build uses the checked-in compiled assets.
+- `node scripts/check-wasm.mjs` checks actual Wasm execution in Node, with no
+  server or browser: RGBA output, batched rendering, changed colors, and reset.
+
+The Wasm module runs in a dedicated module Worker and transfers the completed
+pixel buffer to a canvas. It uses no server rendering service, GPU APIs,
+SharedArrayBuffer, or special cross-origin isolation headers. Randomize changes
+both wall colors and both sphere colors while preserving mirror/glass materials.
+Changing any color, sample count, or resolution starts a new render and cancels
+the previous worker. The Source tab shows the original 99-line C++ implementation.
